<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aragon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of Aragon was a Christian kingdom in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> that took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a> against the Almoravid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. Through union with Catalonia it built a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> presence. The marriage of Ferdinand of Aragon and Isabella of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> in 1469 laid the dynastic foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Aragon" width="320" height="268" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ecelan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reino_de_Arag%C3%B3n.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
